<h1 id="user-content-satisfying-answers"><a class="anchor" href="#satisfying-answers" aria-hidden="true"></a>Satisfying Answers</h1>
<p>I have asked many people many questions, and a lot of them are superficial and meaningless questions whose answers are irrelevant, but there are some questions which you ponder and it is difficult to find a satisfying answer, by that I mean an answer that scratches the itch which the question posed.</p>
<p>I have a few such questions which i am still trying to find satisfying answers for and some for which i have found enough to satisfy me for now</p>
<h2 id="user-content-questions"><a class="anchor" href="#questions" aria-hidden="true"></a>Questions</h2>
<ul>
<li>What does it mean to know someone?</li>
<li>What is happiness?</li>
<li>What is the purpose of travelling?</li>
</ul>
<p>More to come in future...</p>
<h2 id="user-content-answers"><a class="anchor" href="#answers" aria-hidden="true"></a>Answers</h2>
<h4 id="user-content-what-does-it-mean-to-know-someone-x20"><a class="anchor" href="#what-does-it-mean-to-know-someone-x20" aria-hidden="true"></a>What does it mean to know someone?&amp;#x20;</h4>
<p>Very often we say that we have friends or we know someone but to really know someone is really a thin line between the linguistic sense that you know them or that you know of them, so what does it really mean to know someone? The only answer I have been satisfied with so far is:</p>
<p>&amp;#x20;Someone who in any given circumstance you know what they are likely to do</p>
